336
17:37.450 --> 17:39.240
We've never felt that way,

337
17:39.580 --> 17:40.200
okay?

338
17:43.450 --> 17:46.120
But everyone in the neighborhood already knows.

339
18:00.880 --> 18:01.640
Oh.

340
18:01.960 --> 18:03.880
Digging in already?

341
18:04.050 --> 18:05.240
Jeez.

342
18:05.280 --> 18:08.620
I told you to wait for my sour curry, didn't I?

343
18:08.650 --> 18:09.950
You were taking too long.

344
18:09.970 --> 18:10.580
Hey.

345
18:10.860 --> 18:14.860
I had to wait until the sour curry was ready first.

346
18:15.590 --> 18:18.170
How could I let Auntie Daeng's braised pork leg beat my curry?

347
18:22.410 --> 18:23.590
Gear.

348
18:24.460 --> 18:25.960
Eat up, okay?

349
18:27.810 --> 18:29.680
Try not to think about it.

350
18:32.220 --> 18:33.000
Right.

351
18:34.040 --> 18:35.760
Enjoy the food, okay?

352
18:35.980 --> 18:37.360
- Thanks. - No problem.

353
18:39.200 --> 18:40.680
All the dishes here

354
18:41.040 --> 18:43.040
are from our neighbors.

355
18:43.590 --> 18:44.920
They brought them over

356
18:46.060 --> 18:47.880
to show their support for you, Gear.

357
18:48.580 --> 18:50.260
They've known you since you were little.

358
18:50.690 --> 18:52.980
They know what you're like,

359
18:53.770 --> 18:55.780
so they would never believe that video.

360
18:58.050 --> 19:00.180
You're crying again?

361
19:00.580 --> 19:02.170
Whose grandson are you, I wonder?

362
19:02.190 --> 19:03.520
You tear up so easily.

363
19:08.420 --> 19:10.040
Your grandson, of course.

364
19:12.140 --> 19:12.840
Yeah.

365
19:13.930 --> 19:15.700
With all this support,

366
19:15.720 --> 19:18.600
let's figure out how we'll finish all the food.

367
19:19.590 --> 19:20.780
- Exactly. - Come on, come on.

368
19:20.800 --> 19:21.400
Alright.

369
19:21.590 --> 19:22.970
- Eat up, okay? - Let's eat.

370
19:23.180 --> 19:24.680
Come on, what are you waiting for?

371
19:26.250 --> 19:27.560
Let's dig in.

372
19:30.880 --> 19:32.200
Eat well, alright?

373
19:33.000 --> 19:33.570
Eat up.

374
19:33.590 --> 19:35.970
Look at all the support you've got here.

375
19:36.140 --> 19:36.820
See?

376
19:37.840 --> 19:40.260
[One-day Trip]

377
19:40.280 --> 19:43.980
Right now, we're at 'Talat Noi.'

378
19:44.000 --> 19:46.140
This is a riverside community along the Chao Phraya River

379
19:46.160 --> 19:48.780
that still retains its traditional Chinese charm.

380
19:48.800 --> 19:52.120
But there are also cool cafés where we can hang out.

381
19:58.060 --> 20:00.620
My favorite has to be the grilled bananas here.

382
20:00.640 --> 20:01.860
They're grilled just right.

383
20:01.880 --> 20:04.640
If you have time, feel free to visit this community!

384
20:08.760 --> 20:11.610
[inging: Looks very interesting]

385
20:11.630 --> 20:14.680
[milkzii: Did you go there with Gear?]

386
20:21.850 --> 20:24.460
[It's Jay: No, I went there alone]

387
20:24.480 --> 20:27.320
[Sabai Smile: Then who was holding the camera?]

388
20:28.580 --> 20:33.940
[It's Jay: I used a tripod]

389
21:01.000 --> 21:01.920
What's wrong?

390
21:02.170 --> 21:03.630
You look like you need to take a dump.

391
21:05.630 --> 21:06.360
Nothing.

392
21:07.890 --> 21:08.650
Why?

393
21:09.130 --> 21:11.200
Did your boyfriend tell you to hide in the closet again?

394
21:14.540 --> 21:15.310
You can tell us

395
21:15.330 --> 21:17.080
if something's wrong, Nu.

396
21:26.200 --> 21:27.440
There's really nothing, man.

397
21:27.770 --> 21:29.020
It's fine if you don't want to talk.

398
21:30.170 --> 21:31.760
But think about this.

399
21:33.080 --> 21:35.160
Are you really happy right now?

400
21:47.560 --> 21:48.400
Nu.

401
21:49.140 --> 21:51.880
Love should bring you happiness, shouldn't it?

402
21:53.600 --> 21:56.200
If you can't honestly say you're happy,

403
21:56.920 --> 21:59.060
then it's not a healthy relationship, is it?

404
22:06.780 --> 22:08.120
But I love him.

405
22:11.850 --> 22:13.120
Does he love you

406
22:13.420 --> 22:15.020
as much as you love him?

407
22:17.880 --> 22:18.960
If he does,

408
22:19.600 --> 22:21.680
then why are you the one sitting here feeling bad all alone?

409
22:29.880 --> 22:30.640
I think...

410
22:32.200 --> 22:33.400
I should get to work.

411
22:38.690 --> 22:40.400
Zee, wasn't that a bit too harsh?

412
22:41.080 --> 22:41.700
What?

413
22:42.200 --> 22:43.460
I did that for your sake.

414
22:44.040 --> 22:45.920
If he really does break up with that guy,

415
22:45.940 --> 22:47.200
you'll have your chance.

416
22:48.520 --> 22:49.480
Isn't that a good thing?

417
23:00.700 --> 23:02.040
Oh, dear.

418
23:02.280 --> 23:03.720
You almost got thrown in jail overseas

419
23:03.740 --> 23:06.120
all because you were homesick.

420
23:06.500 --> 23:08.360
So how did you handle it, Kanthi?

421
23:09.330 --> 23:11.340
I had to explain to them, of course,

422
23:11.360 --> 23:12.420
that what they were smelling

423
23:12.440 --> 23:13.560
wasn't poisonous gas.

424
23:13.740 --> 23:15.320
I was just making pad kaphrao.

425
23:19.000 --> 23:19.610
Oh, you...

426
23:19.630 --> 23:20.470
Cheers, cheers.

427
23:20.490 --> 23:22.680
There was so much smoke, too.

428
23:23.220 --> 23:24.620
Anyone would be terrified.

429
23:24.820 --> 23:26.010
How about some mangoes?

430
23:29.400 --> 23:30.880
They only got drunk together one night,

431
23:31.400 --> 23:32.780
and they're already this close?

432
23:33.890 --> 23:36.780
Granddad just gets along with everyone easily.

433
23:37.220 --> 23:38.220
It's a good thing, though.

434
23:38.800 --> 23:40.360
This puts my mind at ease.

435
23:52.080 --> 23:53.440
Granddad and Grandpa.

436
23:53.850 --> 23:55.120
- Hello. - Hi.

437
23:55.140 --> 23:55.960
Hello.

438
23:56.020 --> 23:57.320
Mm. Hello.

439
24:00.970 --> 24:01.610
Oh.

440
24:01.630 --> 24:02.560
Come on in.

441
24:07.040 --> 24:08.320
Come on. Come inside.

442
24:09.210 --> 24:10.120
- Alright. - Right.

443
24:11.780 --> 24:12.500
Join us.

444
24:14.400 --> 24:15.230
Gear.

445
24:15.900 --> 24:17.960
How close are you to Mr. Kanthi?

446
24:18.830 --> 24:20.320
You haven't been keeping us updated?

447
24:20.970 --> 24:21.680
Yeah.

448
24:22.490 --> 24:23.880
You said you were done with him.

449
24:25.350 --> 24:27.040
I already gave you two an update, didn't I?

450
24:27.580 --> 24:28.600
Or else...

451
24:28.810 --> 24:30.560
I wouldn't have introduced you to him.

452
24:31.400 --> 24:33.280
So you're officially introducing him to us?

453
24:33.320 --> 24:34.020
Hm?

454
24:34.930 --> 24:36.030
Wait, hold on.

455
24:36.880 --> 24:38.490
You're... serious?

456
24:40.040 --> 24:41.860
But he's a player, though.

457
24:45.620 --> 24:46.650
I think we should drop it.

458
24:47.930 --> 24:49.520
Forget Mr. Kanthi,

459
24:49.840 --> 24:51.240
and let's talk about him.

460
24:52.310 --> 24:55.280
Do you know that video of you punching Sand

461
24:56.060 --> 24:58.320
is all over social media now?

462
24:59.240 --> 24:59.960
What's your plan?

463
25:05.620 --> 25:06.720
I don't know.

464
25:07.480 --> 25:08.640
I have no idea.

465
25:14.730 --> 25:15.830
How about

466
25:16.430 --> 25:17.840
we get revenge on him?

467
25:18.600 --> 25:20.010
And make sure it really hurts.

468
25:22.460 --> 25:23.320
How?

469
25:24.960 --> 25:25.790
Here's what we do.

470
25:26.610 --> 25:27.430
So...

471
25:28.410 --> 25:30.210
Sand really loves Kim, right?

472
25:31.920 --> 25:33.720
Then you steal Kim away from him.

473
25:34.920 --> 25:36.350
Break his heart too.

474
25:37.440 --> 25:39.000
You'll get your boyfriend back

475
25:39.160 --> 25:40.240
and get your revenge too.

476
25:40.270 --> 25:41.840
Killing two birds with one stone.

477
25:41.920 --> 25:43.430
What soap opera have you been watching,

478
25:43.450 --> 25:44.060
hm?

479
25:44.340 --> 25:45.800
It's totally ridiculous.

480
25:46.110 --> 25:47.010
- Huh? - What?

481
25:47.240 --> 25:47.800
Damn you.

482
25:48.880 --> 25:49.760
I won't do it.

483
25:50.240 --> 25:51.780
If I do that,

484
25:55.060 --> 25:56.440
I'm not that different from him, am I?

485
26:07.230 --> 26:09.080
Then, how about...

486
26:09.810 --> 26:12.360
making a video to clear things up?

487
26:12.650 --> 26:14.970
Then we expose him for stealing your boyfriend.

488
26:15.620 --> 26:17.280
That way, people will turn against him.

489
26:17.870 --> 26:19.280
Hey, I think this is a good idea.

490
26:20.200 --> 26:21.040
What do you think?

491
26:21.890 --> 26:22.800
I think it is.

492
26:24.310 --> 26:24.960
Gosh!

493
26:25.580 --> 26:26.840
Nothing I suggest works.

494
26:27.330 --> 26:29.240
I really appreciate you two

495
26:29.620 --> 26:30.800
looking out for me,

496
26:33.390 --> 26:34.640
but just let it go.

497
26:35.900 --> 26:37.350
It'll die down on its own.

498
26:39.230 --> 26:42.790
Things blow over pretty quickly on social media these days.

499
26:43.490 --> 26:46.290
The world might have eyes on me today,

500
26:46.830 --> 26:48.460
but tomorrow, a new controversy will come along,

501
26:48.690 --> 26:49.840
and they'll forget about me.

502
26:50.730 --> 26:51.920
It's up to you then.

503
26:52.910 --> 26:53.560
I'm...

504
26:54.110 --> 26:55.840
I'm so fed up with your kindness.

505
26:56.270 --> 26:57.880
Hey, let me know when you get ordained.

506
26:58.120 --> 26:59.620
I'll come collect some of those coins.

507
27:04.070 --> 27:04.700
Honestly...

508
27:04.720 --> 27:06.920
You don't have to spend the night here with me.

509
27:07.490 --> 27:08.600
I'm really fine.

510
27:10.090 --> 27:11.360
I know you're tough,

511
27:11.850 --> 27:13.800
but isn't it better to have friends by your side?

512
27:14.200 --> 27:14.960
Right, Jay?

513
27:19.490 --> 27:20.330
Damn it, Jay.

514
27:21.000 --> 27:22.790
Why do you look so troubled? What's wrong?

515
27:23.370 --> 27:24.280
It's the netizens.

516
27:24.410 --> 27:26.360
They're going after Gear like he's killed someone.

517
27:26.680 --> 27:28.680
I don't feature you that often on my channel,

518
27:29.200 --> 27:31.160
but they still come after you in almost every video.

519
27:32.600 --> 27:33.760
So fucking annoying.

520
27:34.370 --> 27:35.520
I'm sorry.

521
27:37.080 --> 27:38.640
How is that your fault?

522
27:39.180 --> 27:40.640
It's Sand's fucking fault.

523
27:42.390 --> 27:43.030
Oh, by the way,

524
27:43.750 --> 27:45.010
be honest with me.

525
27:45.950 --> 27:47.450
Back then, how come the two of you...

526
27:47.470 --> 27:48.030
Mm.

527
27:48.200 --> 27:49.440
ever became friends with him?

528
27:49.960 --> 27:51.360
I just don't get it.

529
28:00.160 --> 28:00.670
Wait...

530
28:01.270 --> 28:02.400
That said,

531
28:02.590 --> 28:05.120
some people are taking your side, Gear.

532
28:06.150 --> 28:07.840
Look at this account.

533
28:07.960 --> 28:09.620
It's "KT" or something.

534
28:10.470 --> 28:12.440
He's fighting back against all the hate comments.

535
28:13.490 --> 28:14.200
Take a look.

536
28:15.110 --> 28:15.880
Show me.

537
28:16.030 --> 28:16.590
Look.

538
28:33.000 --> 28:33.680
Gear...

539
28:36.180 --> 28:37.320
Is this your fan?

540
28:47.620 --> 28:49.960
They're insulting his parents, too?!

541
28:50.370 --> 28:51.640
We'll see about that,

542
28:51.850 --> 28:53.000
fucking jackass!

543
28:53.950 --> 28:54.560
Hey.

544
28:54.760 --> 28:55.440
Kanthi.

545
28:55.750 --> 28:58.000
You've been away from the bar for days.

546
28:58.090 --> 28:59.520
Now that I get to see you again,

547
28:59.740 --> 29:01.560
you're just picking fights with people online?

548
29:02.520 --> 29:04.400
Just tell me what you need my help with.

549
29:04.720 --> 29:06.390
I need to get back to looking after the customers.

550
29:06.920 --> 29:08.560
We're already short on waiters today.

551
29:09.400 --> 29:10.400
Fucking hell!

552
29:11.450 --> 29:12.600
Was that for me?

553
29:13.410 --> 29:14.600
I wasn't cursing at you.

554
29:14.640 --> 29:15.880
It's them

555
29:16.440 --> 29:17.840
and their shitty comments.

556
29:18.030 --> 29:19.240
And what were you saying?

557
29:19.530 --> 29:20.530
I wasn't paying attention.

558
29:20.630 --> 29:21.880
For fuck's sake...

559
29:22.770 --> 29:23.900
My question was:

560
29:23.920 --> 29:25.230
What do you need my help with?

561
29:25.620 --> 29:26.720
So you're going to help me?

562
29:34.840 --> 29:36.030
Oh, hey.

563
29:36.650 --> 29:37.850
I got some news last night.

564
29:38.030 --> 29:38.560
What?

565
29:38.720 --> 29:41.080
Kim packed up all his stuff and left Sand's place.

566
29:41.160 --> 29:42.130
Did he?

567
29:42.150 --> 29:42.840
Yeah.

568
29:42.980 --> 29:43.920
Serves him right, huh?

569
29:43.970 --> 29:45.010
Damn right.

570
29:45.030 --> 29:46.840
Acting all tough.

571
29:47.130 --> 29:49.080
In the end, he got dumped.

572
29:49.840 --> 29:51.080
I knew it.

573
29:57.970 --> 30:00.430
What's up, gossipers?

574
30:00.940 --> 30:02.260
Can we have a quick chat?

575
30:02.790 --> 30:03.520
About what?

576
30:04.010 --> 30:05.280
I have nothing to discuss with you guys.

577
30:05.890 --> 30:06.520
Move.

578
30:18.170 --> 30:18.720
Oh...

579
30:18.840 --> 30:19.720
So handsome.

580
30:19.830 --> 30:21.080
He is...

581
30:23.040 --> 30:24.280
Are you the ones

582
30:24.710 --> 30:26.640
who recorded the video of Gear?

583
30:28.560 --> 30:29.870
I'm pretty sure you are

584
30:30.970 --> 30:32.360
because I remember you.

585
30:33.310 --> 30:34.050
Yeah.

586
30:34.770 --> 30:35.800
It's them.

587
30:40.760 --> 30:41.560
Well, then...

588
30:42.970 --> 30:45.320
Can I have a moment with you two?

589
31:08.200 --> 31:09.740
I'm waiting for you at the faculty building.

590
31:09.760 --> 31:12.410
Once you've picked up your stuff from Jay's room, hurry over.

591
31:38.520 --> 31:39.620
What do you want?

592
31:41.730 --> 31:43.620
I came to get a good look at your mug.

593
31:44.250 --> 31:45.760
It's better than I thought, though.

594
31:46.400 --> 31:47.320
I forgot

595
31:47.620 --> 31:49.320
how thick-skinned you are.

596
31:49.780 --> 31:51.010
If I were you

597
31:51.280 --> 31:53.120
and had a scandal like this exposed,

598
31:53.950 --> 31:55.620
I'd have dropped out by now.

599
32:06.680 --> 32:07.620
That's it?

600
32:17.090 --> 32:17.600
Wait.

601
32:17.870 --> 32:18.920
What's the hurry?

602
32:22.760 --> 32:25.080
I came all the way here to give you a chance to apologize.

603
32:26.090 --> 32:27.560
Don't you want to take it?

604
32:27.780 --> 32:28.510
Oh...

605
32:29.720 --> 32:31.320
Or did your Granddad and Grandpa

606
32:31.770 --> 32:32.930
never teach you

607
32:32.950 --> 32:34.120
to say sorry

608
32:34.280 --> 32:35.960
when you do something wrong?

609
32:41.600 --> 32:42.520
Bastard!

610
32:43.400 --> 32:44.730
You can insult me all you like.

611
32:45.230 --> 32:46.720
Don't drag them into this.

612
32:50.410 --> 32:51.230
What?

613
32:51.870 --> 32:53.240
Now you want to apologize to me?

614
32:58.250 --> 32:59.640
Get down and kiss my feet.

615
33:15.410 --> 33:16.030
Hey.

616
33:16.610 --> 33:18.560
You came all the way here to torment him?

617
33:19.580 --> 33:21.310
Good thing you two are here.

618
33:21.810 --> 33:24.350
You can watch him kiss my feet.

619
33:24.940 --> 33:25.560
Sand.

620
33:25.580 --> 33:26.990
Don't you think this is going too far?

621
33:27.930 --> 33:30.330
Why are you making him kiss your feet?

622
33:31.390 --> 33:32.560
Seriously?

623
33:32.870 --> 33:33.600
When you were a kid,

624
33:33.620 --> 33:35.400
did your mom raise you on soap operas?

625
33:35.660 --> 33:38.200
Going around asking people to kiss your feet?

626
33:38.590 --> 33:39.760
What a fucking joke.

627
33:40.160 --> 33:41.150
Stay the fuck out of this.

628
33:42.080 --> 33:43.100
So what if I don't?

629
33:43.120 --> 33:44.100
Jay, Jay, Jay.

630
33:44.120 --> 33:44.720
Don't.

631
33:47.920 --> 33:49.210
You want me to apologize?

632
33:50.600 --> 33:51.480
For what?

633
33:53.310 --> 33:54.440
I did nothing wrong.

634
33:56.530 --> 33:57.920
You know perfectly well

635
33:58.060 --> 33:59.200
what really happened.

636
34:01.000 --> 34:01.830
So what?

637
34:03.270 --> 34:04.570
Other people don't know, though.

638
34:08.170 --> 34:10.040
Can you stop being like this, Sand?

639
34:11.170 --> 34:12.239
Aren't you tired?

640
34:13.050 --> 34:14.360
Because I fucking am.

641
34:15.620 --> 34:17.560
Can't we just go our separate ways?

642
34:18.370 --> 34:20.370
Then keep looking on the bright side.

643
34:20.909 --> 34:21.800
Just think of this

644
34:22.190 --> 34:24.560
as the karma you've brought upon yourself.

645
34:28.760 --> 34:30.010
What's so fucking funny?

646
34:30.449 --> 34:31.400
My bad.

647
34:32.239 --> 34:32.920
It's just...

648
34:33.449 --> 34:34.590
Listening to you talk

649
34:34.960 --> 34:36.440
is like watching one of those morality dramas.

650
34:36.960 --> 34:38.489
By the way...

651
34:38.510 --> 34:39.760
what Gear experienced

652
34:40.389 --> 34:41.639
isn't karma.

653
34:42.840 --> 34:44.310
Because what karma really is

654
34:46.120 --> 34:47.360
comes after this.

655
34:48.280 --> 34:49.639
What the hell are you talking about?

656
34:59.250 --> 35:00.080
Speak!

657
35:04.230 --> 35:05.320
Well... Well...

658
35:05.450 --> 35:08.050
Based on the start of the video, it may seem like...

659
35:08.070 --> 35:09.480
Gear started it first, right?

660
35:09.500 --> 35:10.250
But...

661
35:10.680 --> 35:12.560
Gear was really drunk that night.

662
35:12.580 --> 35:13.160
And...

663
35:13.390 --> 35:15.600
the incident was actually caused by Sand.

664
35:15.620 --> 35:17.370
He stole Gear's boyfriend

665
35:17.390 --> 35:19.520
and mocked him at the bar.

666
35:19.880 --> 35:20.750
Ex... Exactly.

667
35:20.770 --> 35:22.880
That video was filmed over a month ago.

668
35:23.170 --> 35:25.710
Sand saw that Gear was going viral.

669
35:25.730 --> 35:26.270
Yes.

